
@base = http://localhost:8080
@freeKey = demo-free-key
@proKey = demo-pro-key
@adminKey = demo-admin-key
# business clients: online storefront, supplier (partner), warehouse scanner
@storefrontKey = demo-storefront-key
@supplierKey = demo-supplier-key
@scannerKey = demo-scanner-key


### 1. Gateway readiness (Redis + Postgres)
GET {{base}}/ready


### 2a. Stock service requires auth  ->  401
GET {{base}}/api/stock/movements


### 2b. Wrong key  ->  401
GET {{base}}/api/stock/movements
x-api-key: wrong-key


### 2c. Valid key  ->  200
GET {{base}}/api/stock/movements?limit=10
x-api-key: {{proKey}}


### 3. Get a JWT
# @name login
POST {{base}}/auth/token
x-api-key: {{proKey}}


### 3b. Use the JWT instead of the key
GET {{base}}/api/stock/movements?limit=5
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}


### 4. INVENTORY - list all items (cached 5 s by the gateway: repeat it and see X-Cache: HIT)
GET {{base}}/api/inventory
x-api-key: {{proKey}}


### 4b. Filters: category, search, stock status (low,out), a single warehouse
GET {{base}}/api/inventory?category=Electronics&status=low,out
x-api-key: {{proKey}}

###
GET {{base}}/api/inventory?q=box&warehouse=WH-NORTH
x-api-key: {{proKey}}


### 4c. One SKU (bypassing the cache)
GET {{base}}/api/inventory/ELE-1001
x-api-key: {{proKey}}
Cache-Control: no-cache


### 4d. Dashboard summary: totals, per warehouse, per category, reorder alerts
GET {{base}}/api/inventory/summary
x-api-key: {{proKey}}


### 4e. Warehouses
GET {{base}}/api/inventory/warehouses
x-api-key: {{proKey}}


### 4f. Create an item  ->  201 (409 if the SKU exists). Stock starts at 0 everywhere.
POST {{base}}/api/inventory
x-api-key: {{scannerKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "sku": "ELE-1099",
  "name": "Webcam HD",
  "category": "Electronics",
  "unitCost": 49.99,
  "reorderLevel": 20
}


### 4g. Update item metadata
PATCH {{base}}/api/inventory/ELE-1099
x-api-key: {{scannerKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "reorderLevel": 25 }


### 5. STOCK - receive goods  ->  201. Also purges the inventory cache (request 4 -> MISS)
POST {{base}}/api/stock/receive
x-api-key: {{supplierKey}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: po-1001-line-1

{ "sku": "ELE-1099", "warehouse": "WH-NORTH", "qty": 50, "reference": "PO-1001" }


### 5b. Same request, same Idempotency-Key  ->  200 + idempotent-replay: true (not applied twice)
POST {{base}}/api/stock/receive
x-api-key: {{supplierKey}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: po-1001-line-1

{ "sku": "ELE-1099", "warehouse": "WH-NORTH", "qty": 50, "reference": "PO-1001" }


### 5c. Ship  ->  201
POST {{base}}/api/stock/ship
x-api-key: {{storefrontKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "sku": "ELE-1099", "warehouse": "WH-NORTH", "qty": 8, "reference": "SO-5001" }


### 5d. Ship more than is on hand  ->  409 insufficient_stock (never goes negative)
POST {{base}}/api/stock/ship
x-api-key: {{storefrontKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "sku": "ELE-1099", "warehouse": "WH-NORTH", "qty": 9999 }


### 5e. Transfer between warehouses (atomic)
POST {{base}}/api/stock/transfer
x-api-key: {{scannerKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "sku": "ELE-1099", "from": "WH-NORTH", "to": "WH-SOUTH", "qty": 10 }


### 5f. Cycle-count adjustment (delta may be negative)
POST {{base}}/api/stock/adjust
x-api-key: {{scannerKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "sku": "ELE-1099", "warehouse": "WH-SOUTH", "delta": -1, "reason": "damaged unit" }


### 5g. Movement history for a SKU
GET {{base}}/api/stock/movements?sku=ELE-1099
x-api-key: {{proKey}}


### 5h. Movements per minute (dashboard chart)
GET {{base}}/api/stock/throughput?minutes=10
x-api-key: {{proKey}}


### 5i. Consistency audit: every stock level == sum of its ledger entries, none negative
GET {{base}}/api/stock/audit
x-api-key: {{adminKey}}


### 5k. PERMISSIONS - a supplier may only receive stock: shipping  ->  403 forbidden
POST {{base}}/api/stock/ship
x-api-key: {{supplierKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "sku": "ELE-1099", "warehouse": "WH-NORTH", "qty": 1 }


### 5l. ...and the storefront may not adjust stock  ->  403 forbidden
POST {{base}}/api/stock/adjust
x-api-key: {{storefrontKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "sku": "ELE-1099", "warehouse": "WH-NORTH", "delta": 100 }


### 5j. Delete an item (admin only)
DELETE {{base}}/api/inventory/ELE-1099
x-api-key: {{adminKey}}


### 6. RATE LIMITING - send this quickly 20+ times with the free key  ->  429
GET {{base}}/api/inventory/ELE-1002
x-api-key: {{freeKey}}


### 7. TIMEOUT - the backend sleeps 4 s, the gateway waits max 3 s  ->  504 Gateway Timeout
GET {{base}}/api/inventory/slow?ms=4000
x-api-key: {{proKey}}


### 8a. CHAOS - make inventory-2 fail every request (circuit opens, traffic moves to 1 and 3)
POST {{base}}/admin/instances/inventory-2/chaos
x-api-key: {{adminKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "failRate": 1 }


### 8b. Check the status of all services
GET {{base}}/admin/services
x-api-key: {{adminKey}}


### 8c. Kill inventory-3 completely (health checks will mark it DOWN after ~6 s)
POST {{base}}/admin/instances/inventory-3/chaos
x-api-key: {{adminKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "down": true }


### 8d. Repair both instances
POST {{base}}/admin/instances/inventory-2/chaos
x-api-key: {{adminKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "reset": true }

###
POST {{base}}/admin/instances/inventory-3/chaos
x-api-key: {{adminKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "reset": true }


### 9. LOGS saved in PostgreSQL by the workers (latest 10 requests)
GET {{base}}/admin/logs?limit=10
x-api-key: {{adminKey}}


### 9b. Only the errors (5xx)
GET {{base}}/admin/logs?status=5xx&limit=10
x-api-key: {{adminKey}}


### 9c. Only the rate-limited requests (429)
GET {{base}}/admin/logs?status=429&limit=10
x-api-key: {{adminKey}}


### 9d. Only stock-service traffic
GET {{base}}/admin/logs?service=stock&limit=10
x-api-key: {{adminKey}}


### 10. Statistics (the same data the gateway dashboard shows)
GET {{base}}/admin/stats
x-api-key: {{adminKey}}


### 11. Clear the whole cache
POST {{base}}/admin/cache/purge
x-api-key: {{adminKey}}
